            Every pick below is a powered rotor desiccant dehumidifier, not a rechargeable silica canister, and every one was in stock on Amazon US when we checked. We have not lab-tested these units; the specifications come from manufacturer spec sheets, user manuals and retailer listings, and where those sources disagree we say so. All four are domestic condensing units that collect water in a tank or drain hose. Ducted industrial desiccant machines that keep working below freezing exist, from brands such as Ebac and Ecor Pro, but we could not find them reliably in stock on Amazon, so they are covered in the text rather than ranked.
          </p>

